# ShieldScan Permanent Project Rules

1. Follow the approved plan (stack, folder structure, design system) exactly. Do not change the stack without asking me.
2. Premium quality bar: every UI must feel like Linear / Vercel / Stripe level polish. No generic template look, no default unstyled components.
3. Use TypeScript strictly, no `any`. Reusable components, clean separation of UI / logic / services.
4. Every page and component must be responsive (mobile-first), accessible (WCAG AA, keyboard + aria), and support dark and light mode through design tokens, never hardcoded colors.
5. Every async UI needs loading, empty, and error states.
6. Never hardcode secrets. Use env variables and keep `.env.example` updated.
7. Security first: validate all inputs with Zod, protect against SSRF on any user-supplied URL, rate limit public endpoints.
8. Work in small steps. After each task: run lint and type-check, fix errors, then summarize what you did and what I should test. Do not start the next phase until I say so.
9. Use only real, working code. No placeholder lorem ipsum in final UI copy; write real, persuasive product copy.
